<!-- What the OBS package home:jmbriccola:porthole/porthole holds instead of
     its sources: the two services that fetch them.

     A release tagged on GitHub carries one attachment, obs-sources.tar, with
     the seven files packaging/obs/make-sources.sh produces. download_url
     takes the newest release's copy of it, and extract_file unpacks all
     seven beside it. OBS then builds the spec for the Fedora repositories
     and the .dsc for the Debian ones, exactly as it does from files uploaded
     by hand.

     The release is made by .github/workflows/ci.yml, only for a tag and only
     once every job of that run is green. The same job then asks OBS to run
     these services, with a token that can do nothing else and nothing to any
     other package.

     filename is set because the service otherwise stores the file under the
     name the server reports: fetching a tag tarball by hand here left a
     v1.0.1.tar.gz. The files parameter is a glob, which extract_file hands to
     tar, so nothing in this file names a version and no release has to edit
     it. -->
<services>
  <service name="download_url">
    <param name="url">https://github.com/jmbriccola/porthole/releases/latest/download/obs-sources.tar</param>
    <param name="filename">obs-sources.tar</param>
  </service>
  <service name="extract_file">
    <param name="archive">obs-sources.tar</param>
    <param name="files">*</param>
  </service>
</services>
